{
  "description": "core §2.7 (0.24), a population: a resource's `kind`, its `bound` (an integer, \"no_ceiling\" or \"untemplated\"), an event's `retention_s`, and one reading → whether the instance holds more live members than its bound (`expect.verdict`: exceeds, within, unobservable or not_asked) and the reason class (`expect.reason`). A reading is an owner's S4 GET of a state resource (`via: get`: how many keys it answered with a value, and whether it ran to its final reply) or a subscription window over a stream or an event (`via: window`: per member, the seconds at which it was heard, on one clock). A window counts the most members heard within any span shorter than the liveness period, an hour for a stream and the retention for an event: two instants exactly one period apart are not within it. Reasons are chosen in this order: not_asked (kind: an operation; no_ceiling; untemplated); unobservable reading_kind (a window of a state, a GET of a stream or an event); exceeds over_bound (in any reading); unobservable empty (no member, O5); unobservable incomplete (a GET that did not run to its final reply) or window; within complete.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "note": "a complete GET within the bound: clean",
      "kind": "state",
      "bound": 8,
      "retention_s": null,
      "reading": {
        "via": "get",
        "members": 5,
        "complete": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "verdict": "within",
        "reason": "complete"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "exactly the bound is within it",
      "kind": "state",
      "bound": 8,
      "retention_s": null,
      "reading": {
        "via": "get",
        "members": 8,
        "complete": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "verdict": "within",
        "reason": "complete"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "one more than the bound: the finding",
      "kind": "state",
      "bound": 8,
      "retention_s": null,
      "reading": {
        "via": "get",
        "members": 9,
        "complete": true
      },
      "expect": {
        "verdict": "exceeds",
        "reason": "over_bound"
      }
    },
    {
